Subject: simple IPA: re-trigger autofocus when the scene changes

The contrast-detection autofocus locked and then only rescanned when the focus
score dropped below 70% of the locked value for five statistics, or after
about a minute. That misses the common case of the subject moving away: a lens
focused near blurs everything else, so the score stays low and never "drops",
and the picture stays blurry.

While locked, compare each statistics frame with a reference taken a few
statistics after the lock: the luminance histogram (total-variation distance
above 0.25) or the focus score (outside 0.6x-1.6x) changing for two
consecutive statistics marks the scene as changed. Wait until it holds still
(consecutive histograms within 0.10, or a bounded wait of 16 statistics) and
then scan again, so a hand moving through the frame is not chased. The old
triggers are kept. Thresholds are first guesses and untuned; the metrics are
logged at debug level (IPASoft) to tune them.

